    function copyMarginPreferences(srcPage, dstPage) {
        try {
            dstPage.marginPreferences.top = srcPage.marginPreferences.top;
            dstPage.marginPreferences.bottom = srcPage.marginPreferences.bottom;
            dstPage.marginPreferences.left = srcPage.marginPreferences.left;
            dstPage.marginPreferences.right = srcPage.marginPreferences.right;

            try { dstPage.marginPreferences.columnCount = srcPage.marginPreferences.columnCount; } catch (_) {}
            try { dstPage.marginPreferences.columnGutter = srcPage.marginPreferences.columnGutter; } catch (_) {}
            try { dstPage.marginPreferences.columnsPositions = srcPage.marginPreferences.columnsPositions; } catch (_) {}
        } catch (_) {}
    }

    function copyGuides(srcPage, dstPage) {
        try {
            var guides = srcPage.guides.everyItem().getElements();
            for (var i = 0; i < guides.length; i++) {
                guides[i].duplicate(dstPage);
            }
        } catch (_) {}
    }

    function getPageSideCode(pg) {
        try {
            switch (pg.side) {
                case PageSideOptions.LEFT_HAND:
                    return "L";
                case PageSideOptions.RIGHT_HAND:
                    return "R";
                default:
                    return "S";
            }
        } catch (_) {
            return "S";
        }
    }

    function sideLabel(code) {
        if (code === "L") return "Left";
        if (code === "R") return "Right";
        return "Single";
    }

    function tryDeleteUnusedDefaultMaster(defaultMaster, dstDoc) {
        if (!defaultMaster || !defaultMaster.isValid) return;

        try {
            var used = false;
            var pages = dstDoc.pages.everyItem().getElements();

            for (var i = 0; i < pages.length; i++) {
                try {
                    if (pages[i].appliedMaster && pages[i].appliedMaster.isValid && pages[i].appliedMaster.id === defaultMaster.id) {
                        used = true;
                        break;
                    }
                } catch (_) {}
            }

            if (!used) {
                defaultMaster.remove();
            }
        } catch (_) {}
    }

})();
```

---

## What this script does well

It preserves:

- page order
- page size
- page margins
- column settings
- page guides
- layers
- most object positions
- master-page relationship, by converting each left/right master page into its own single-page master

Example:

- source master spread `A-Master` with left and right pages
- destination gets:
  - `AL / A-Master [Left]`
  - `AR / A-Master [Right]`

Then:
- former left-hand document pages get the `[Left]` single-page master
- former right-hand document pages get the `[Right]` single-page master

This is the cleanest way to preserve master references in a non-facing-pages document.

---

## Important limitations

Because InDesign facing-page masters and single-page masters are structurally different, there are a few unavoidable caveats:

1. **Master spreads cannot remain literally the same objects**
   - They must be recreated as single-page masters.
   - The script preserves the functional relationship, not the original master-spread object identity.

2. **Some complex objects may need manual checking**
   - anchored objects
   - text variables with spread-specific behavior
   - objects relying on spine-relative settings
   - cross-spread items
   - special interactive objects

3. **Paragraph/object styles, swatches, etc.**
   - In most cases, duplicating items into the new document brings dependencies along automatically.
   - If your file is very complex, you may want a version that explicitly copies styles/swatches too.

4. **Sections, numbering, bookmarks, hyperlinks, TOC, XML, scripts labels**
   - not copied in this version unless they are attached to duplicated items
   - can be added if needed

---

## Best practice before using

- duplicate your InDesign file first
- run on a copy
- visually inspect:
  - left/right pages
  - pages with overridden master items
  - pages with anchored objects
  - pages with items crossing the spine

